From: Anaconda recipe maintenance <pkg-team@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win-arm64: shard python_functions + disable optimizer on binding glue

The generated python_functions_N.cpp autograd-binding TUs each need ~15GB to
compile with the MSVC /O2 optimizer targeting arm64 (template-instantiation
blowup), exceeding the 16GB PBP win-arm64 worker memory watchdog. Empirically
the peak is a FIXED per-TU cost: halving shard content and serializing
compiles left the peak unchanged at ~15.6GB (pytorch-feedstock#118 smoke 3-10),
proving the cost is optimizer memory on the generated code, not scheduling or
file size.

Fix, win-arm64-only via meta.yaml patch selector:
  1. num_shards 5->10 (gen_autograd_functions.py) + the matching hardcoded
     GENERATED_CXX_PYTHON list in caffe2/CMakeLists.txt (both are sources of
     truth for the shard count; the CMake list is what actually gets compiled,
     so a mismatch silently drops autograd registrations).
  2. /Od on the generated Python-binding TUs (set_source_files_properties):
     these are registration glue, not perf-critical, so disabling the
     optimizer removes the ~15GB spike with no meaningful runtime cost.

The python_torch_functions_* count stays at 3 (must sync with
gatherTorchFunctions) and is not the hotspot.

diff --git a/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt b/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
index bf0e3f0..6e1fb77 100644
--- a/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -292,6 +292,11 @@ set(GENERATED_CXX_PYTHON
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_2.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_3.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_4.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_5.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_6.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_7.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_8.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_9.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_variable_methods.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_torch_functions_0.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_torch_functions_1.cpp"
@@ -307,6 +312,17 @@ set(GENERATED_CXX_PYTHON
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/functionalization/generated/ViewMetaClassesPythonBinding.cpp"
   )
 
+# win-arm64 memory workaround: the generated Python-binding TUs are autograd
+# registration glue (not perf-critical); under MSVC/arm64 the /O2 optimizer
+# needs ~15GB per shard (template instantiation blowup), over the 16GB PBP
+# worker memory watchdog. /Od removes that optimizer spike.
+if(MSVC)
+  set_source_files_properties(
+    ${GENERATED_CXX_PYTHON}
+    PROPERTIES COMPILE_FLAGS "/Od"
+  )
+endif()
+
 set(GENERATED_H_PYTHON
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions.h"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_return_types.h"
diff --git a/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py b/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py
index 002a551..2a6471b 100644
--- a/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py
+++ b/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py
@@ -568,7 +568,7 @@ def gen_autograd_functions_python(
     template_path: str,
 ) -> None:
     fm = FileManager(install_dir=out, template_dir=template_path, dry_run=False)
-    num_shards = 5
+    num_shards = 10
     fm.write(
         "python_functions.h",
         lambda: {
